{"step_index":577,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:15:45Z","input_tokens":2787,"cache_read_tokens":112775,"output_tokens":2681,"thinking":"Phase four involves interactive learning, specifically a quiz and prediction card component. The focus shifts to designing `renderInteractiveQuiz`, which necessitates careful consideration of how the `step` and `currentSubstep` data will be utilized to generate the quiz content. This stage aims to make the learning more active, reinforcing the concepts through engagement.\n\n\nThe `renderInteractiveQuiz` function needs to handle quiz rendering based on the step data. It should check if the quiz is enabled and if a question exists for the current step. If not, it hides the quiz card. When a quiz appears during autoplay, it pauses the animation if the learner has not answered. I'm thinking of rendering the quiz card and displaying the question number and score.\n\n\nQuiz option buttons must reflect answer state; correct answers should be visually distinct. Answered questions require feedback display, which includes a heading based on the answer's correctness and an explanation. Correct and incorrect answer buttons are styled differently to indicate the correct and user-selected option.\n\n\nThe quiz card content is dynamically generated based on whether the question has been answered. If answered, a \"Continue Step\" button appears; otherwise, \"Skip & Reveal\" is shown. The HTML is assembled to display the question, context, options, feedback, and action buttons. Option click handlers are attached to unanswered questions, linking the clicked index to an event listener.\n\n\nQuiz answers are tracked by updating the `quizAnswers` map with the selected option index, correctness, and answer status.  Click events on option buttons increment the total and correct quiz scores based on the `isCorrect` property of the selected option.  The `renderStep` method is called to refresh the quiz display after an answer is submitted or skipped.\n\nKeyboard shortcuts '1', '2', '3', '4' can automatically select an option when quiz mode is enabled and a question is present.\n\n\nKeyboard input for quiz selection is working correctly, confirming the design for interactive element responses. Reviewing the restart functionality, it must clear quiz answers and reset the score to allow fresh attempts. The restart button's click handler now includes a clear for quiz answers and resets the quiz score upon re-initialization.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js","EndLine":65,"StartLine":30,"toolAction":"Viewing app.js constructor and initDOM","toolSummary":"View app.js constructor and initDOM"}}]}
