{"step_index":623,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:20:05Z","input_tokens":2717,"cache_read_tokens":142955,"output_tokens":1840,"content":"### Implementation Complete: Phase 4 — Interactive Learning (Predict Mode)\n\nWe have implemented **Phase 4 — Add Interactive Learning** in the Code Flow Visualizer, allowing learners to predict execution outcomes before key calculation and decision steps, test their intuition, and immediately see the correct results with detailed explanations.\n\n---\n\n### Files Modified\n\n| File | Changes Made |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| [index.html](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html) | Added the **`🎯 Quiz Mode: OFF / ON`** toggle button in the top navigation bar and added the `#predictQuizCard` interactive container in Area 2 directly below the current code line. |\n| [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css) | Added styling for the prediction card (`.predict-quiz-card`), violet header badge, live score chip (`Score: X/Y ⭐`), option buttons (`.quiz-option-btn`), correct/wrong answer states (`.is-correct`, `.is-wrong`), explanation boxes, and mobile responsive layout. |\n| [explainer.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js) | Implemented the rule-based prediction question generator (`buildPredictionQuestion`) that attaches questions and plausible distractors to selected execution steps. |\n| [app.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js) | Added quiz state tracking (`quizAnswers`, `quizScore`), toggle logic, keyboard shortcuts (`1`, `2`, `3`, `4`), option click evaluation, instant feedback with explanation revealing, and Auto Play pausing during questions. |\n\n---\n\n### Key Features & Mechanics\n\n#### 1. Learner Predictions Before Key Steps\nBefore key operational and decision steps, an interactive card prompts the learner to predict the outcome:\n- **\"What will `c` become after this addition?\"**\n  - Prompted on lines like `c += nums[i]`.\n  - Context shows the previous value of `c` and the element being added (e.g., `c = 0` and adding `1`).\n  - Generates plausible multiple-choice options (the correct sum, un-added previous value, replaced operand, or sign variation).\n- **\"Will this condition be True or False?\"**\n  - Prompted on conditional branches like `if c < 0:` or `if c >= ans:`.\n  - Context shows actual values (e.g., comparing `-2 < 0`).\n  - Options: `True` or `False`.\n- **\"Will `ans` change?\"**\n  - Prompted during record checks like `if c >= ans:`.\n  - Options: `Yes, ans will update to <new_val>` vs. `No, ans stays <curr_val>`.\n- **Kadane's Reset & Final Return:**\n  - On `c = 0` after a negative running total: asks learners why `c` resets to `0` (discarding negative prefix).\n  - On the final return statement: asks learners to predict the final maximum subarray sum.\n\n#### 2. Instant Feedback & Explanation Reveal\n- Clicking an option immediately reveals:\n  - **Correct Answer**: Highlighted in emerald green with a `✓ Your Answer` badge and a celebration message.\n  - **Incorrect Answer**: Highlighted in soft red with a `✗ Your Answer` badge, while simultaneously revealing the correct answer.\n  - **Detailed Explanation**: Displays a breakdown of why the calculation or comparison resulted in that outcome.\n  - **Continue Button (`Continue Step ➔`)**: Lets the learner proceed directly to the next substep to watch the animated memory and value updates.\n  - **Skip & Reveal Button**: Allows learners to bypass guessing and immediately inspect the answer.\n\n#### 3. Completely Optional (`🎯 Quiz Mode: OFF / ON`)\n- **Default State**: Off. Stepping, F7 Sub-expr, and Auto Play operate uninterrupted.\n- **When Toggled On**:\n  - The button turns violet with active styling (`🎯 Quiz Mode: ON`).\n  - Selected decision and calculation steps pause with the interactive question card.\n  - If Auto Play is running when a question is reached, it automatically pauses to give the learner time to think.\n  - The live score tracker displays their accuracy (e.g., `Score: 3/4 (75%) ⭐`).\n  - Toggling off at any time instantly dismisses the card and resumes standard stepping.\n\n#### 4. Keyboard & Mobile Accessibility\n- Learners on desktops can press keys **`1`**, **`2`**, **`3`**, or **`4`** to quickly select options.\n- On mobile devices and tablets, option buttons expand into full-width touch cards for tap navigation.","thinking":"Checking `index.html` to confirm the presence of the quiz toggle button in the header and the quiz card div in Area 2. Then, examining `styles.css` to verify the completion of the Phase 4 styling.\n\n\nAnaly